---
title: "Switch"
description: "Toggle for on/off settings, built on a native checkbox."
tags: [forms, accessibility, css]
usage: |
  Put an `<input type="checkbox" role="switch">` and its text inside a `<label>`
  with the `switch` class. It submits with forms like any checkbox. Use it for
  settings that take effect immediately; use a plain checkbox in forms that are
  submitted.
accessibility: |
  - `role="switch"` makes screen readers announce it as on or off rather than
    checked or not checked.
  - The label wraps the input, so clicking the text toggles it, and Space works
    from the keyboard.
  - A visible outline is drawn on keyboard focus.
  - The thumb does not animate when the person prefers reduced motion.
customProperties:
  "--switch-gap": "Space between the switch and its text."
  "--switch-inline-size": "Width of the track."
  "--switch-block-size": "Height of the track."
  "--switch-thumb-inset": "Space between the thumb and the track edge."
  "--switch-track": "Track color when off."
  "--switch-track-checked": "Track color when on."
  "--switch-thumb": "Thumb color."
  "--switch-duration": "Length of the thumb animation."
  "--switch-easing": "Timing function of the animation."
  "--switch-focus-ring": "Outline shown on keyboard focus."
---

<link rel="stylesheet" href="./styles.css" media="screen">

<label class="switch">
  <input type="checkbox" role="switch" name="notifications">
  <span>Notifications</span>
</label>
